          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Suppose a principal of $100,000 is deposited into an account with an annual interest rate of 3% for five years. Find the final balance if interest is compounded annually, quarterly, monthly, weekly and every second. Use 52 weeks per year for weekly compounding and 365 days per year for per-second compounding. Round each balance to the nearest cent. Describe the trend as the compounding periods shorten. Does the balance appear to approach a limit as the periods continue to shorten?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Annually $\\$115{,}927.41$, quarterly $\\$116{,}118.41$, monthly $\\$116{,}161.68$, weekly $\\$116{,}178.40$, and every second $\\$116{,}183.42$. The balance increases and appears to approach a limit of about $\\$116{,}183.42$.",
      "worked": "With $P=100{,}000$, $r=0.03$ and $t=5$, the number of periods per year is $1$, $4$, $12$, $52$ or $365\\times24\\times60\\times60=31{,}536{,}000$, respectively. Write $A(n)$ for the balance when interest is compounded $n$ times per year.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A(1)&=\\$100{,}000(1+0.03)^5\\approx\\$115{,}927.41\\\\ A(4)&=\\$100{,}000\\left(1+\\frac{0.03}{4}\\right)^{20}\\approx\\$116{,}118.41\\\\ A(12)&=\\$100{,}000\\left(1+\\frac{0.03}{12}\\right)^{60}\\approx\\$116{,}161.68\\\\ A(52)&=\\$100{,}000\\left(1+\\frac{0.03}{52}\\right)^{260}\\approx\\$116{,}178.40\\\\ A(31{,}536{,}000)&=\\$100{,}000\\left(1+\\frac{0.03}{31{,}536{,}000}\\right)^{157{,}680{,}000}\\\\ A(31{,}536{,}000)&\\approx\\$116{,}183.42\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe balances increase as the periods shorten. The weekly and per-second balances are only about five dollars apart, and the values suggest a limit near $\\$116{,}183.42$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 35
  },
